' ----- DUP-9: tray-icon refresh single funnel -----
package "DUP-9  Tray icon refresh" $TINT_RESOLVED {
  [App.RequestTrayRefresh\n(single funnel)] as D9X
  [TrayIconPresenter.Refresh\n(only invoked via D9X)] as D9Y
  D9X -[#green]- D9Y : startup, theme, settings,\ntopology, brightness, scroll all\nflow through RequestTrayRefresh
}

' ----- DUP-10 PARTIAL: timer inventory -----
package "DUP-10  Timer inventory" $TINT_PARTIAL {
  [DisplayEventManager._coalesce\n(DispatcherTimer, 250 ms)] as D10A
  [DisplayEventManager._burstTimer\n(System.Threading.Timer, 1 s x 10)] as D10B
  [EnvironmentalCurveService._curveTimer\n(DispatcherTimer)] as D10C
  [DDCRecoveryService fallback worker\n(Task.Delay loop only while\nDDC candidates exist)] as D10D
  [NightLightRegistry._resendTimer\n(System.Threading.Timer, debounced resend)] as D10E
  [DisplayIdentifierService._timer\n(DispatcherTimer, overlay auto-hide)] as D10F
  [TADNLog flush timer\n(Common, async flush)] as D10G
  [NightLightSettingsHandler._deferredRegistryTimer\n(System.Threading.Timer; 6089fd8 NL flicker-fix)] as D10I
  [KnownDisplaysStore._stampDebounceTimer\n(System.Threading.Timer)] as D10J
  [BrightnessFlyout._previewSweepTimer\n(DispatcherTimer, 50 ms cadence)] as D10L
  [TrayAppDotNETAboutPage._staleTimer\n(Common, DispatcherTimer)] as D10M
  [EnvironmentalCurveEditor._currentTimeTimer\n(DispatcherTimer)] as D10N
  [EnvironmentalPage._curveSaveDebounceTimer\n(DispatcherTimer)] as D10O
  note bottom
    Each timer owns a distinct domain.
    The tray icon presenter is event-driven (no internal timer);
    taskbar re-creation is handled by the Common shell tray icon.
    PARTIAL: the threading-timer callbacks guard their own
    exceptions, but the inventory is still not documented
    outside this map.
  end note
}

' ----- DUP-11 PARTIAL: hex color parsing (theme and overrides share ColorMath; the picker keeps its own) -----
package "DUP-11  Hex color parsing / formatting" $TINT_PARTIAL {
  [Common Utils/ColorMath.cs\n.TryParseHexOrNull / .ParseHexStrict] as D11X
  [Common Visuals/AppTheme.cs\n(strict: throws on bad input)] as D11A
  [Common UI/Models/NullableThemeColor.cs\n(user overrides: nullable)] as D11B
  [Common UI/Controls/ColorPickerWindow.cs\n.TryParseHex (ARGB or RGBA order,\n3/4/6/8-char input)] as D11C
  D11X -[#green]- D11A : shared primitive
  D11X -[#green]- D11B : shared primitive
  D11X -[#orange]- D11C : picker accepts short forms\nand both byte orders
  note bottom
    The theme and override paths share one parser with
    two error policies. The picker's text boxes still
    parse on their own because they accept short forms
    and ARGB / RGBA order.
  end note
}

' ----- DUP-12 PARTIAL: monitor-id prefix vocabulary -----
package "DUP-12  Monitor-id prefix vocabulary" $TINT_PARTIAL {
  [MonitorService.ComputeEDIDKey /\nComputePortFormKey\n(produce edid: / port: / num:)] as D12A
  [MonitorService\n(PortKeyPrefix const + inline\n"edid:" / "port:" StartsWith checks)] as D12B
  [Models/Hotkey.cs HotkeyTarget\n(EDIDPrefix const "edid:")] as D12C
  [DDCCI/DisplayService.cs\n(own instance: / edid: / name: keys)] as D12D
  D12A -[#orange]- D12B : producer / consumer
  D12A -[#orange]- D12C : same literal,\nseparate const
  note bottom
    The "edid:" / "port:" / "num:" tokens
    are produced in one place but each consumer
    re-declares its own const string for the
    prefix it cares about. Cheap to share via
    a small MonitorIdPrefixes static.
  end note
}

' ----- DUP-13 RESOLVED: hotkey paths route through Notify*Adjustment helper -----
package "DUP-13  Hotkey vs tray-scroll Notify discipline" $TINT_RESOLVED {
  [App.cs:AdjustAllMonitorBrightness\nApp.cs:AdjustNightLightBrightness\nApp.cs:ApplyOrRestoreBrightness] as D13A
  [App.cs:OnTrayScrolled] as D13B
  [Notify*Adjustment helpers\n(App.cs + BrightnessFlyoutWindow,\nsingle funnel)] as D13C
  D13A -[#green]- D13C : all hotkey paths now\ncall NotifyUserBrightnessAdjustment /\nNotifyUserNightLightAdjustment
  D13B -[#green]- D13C : tray scroll routes through\nthe same helper
  note bottom
    Wave-1 fix: hotkey and tray-scroll write paths
    share the same release-discipline funnel.
    Curve toggle stays lit while individuals
    auto-release consistently across both entry
    points (H-05 closed).
  end note
}

' ----- DUP-16 PARTIAL: acquisition state reconciliation still has parallel arms -----
package "DUP-16  DDC acquisition state reconciliation" $TINT_PARTIAL {
  [RefreshProbePhaseAsync\nnew-row + existing-row\npromotion arms] as D16A
  [PromoteRecovered] as D16B
  [PromoteReadDegraded] as D16C
  D16A -[#orange]- D16B : repeat metadata, entry, projection,\ncapability, and slider-state ordering
  D16B -[#orange]- D16C : share most publication steps\nbut differ in confirmation state
  note bottom
    Correct today, but both capability publication and recovered
    post-subscriber ownership ordering have drifted before.
    Fully readable replay is now centralized after MonitorsRefreshed;
    entry installation and degraded publication remain duplicated.
    Plan: one private dispatcher-only publication method
    accepting a small acquisition result and New / Recovered /
    ReadDegraded mode. Keep enumeration and DDC I/O outside it.
  end note
}

' ----- DUP-18 RESOLVED: brightness percent -> raw VCP scaling -----
package "DUP-18  Brightness percent -> raw VCP scaling" $TINT_RESOLVED {
  [MonitorService.ScaleBrightnessPercentToRaw\nsingle pct -> raw helper] as D18X
  [MonitorService.DoBrightnessWriteAsync\nuses entry.Max] as D18A
  [MonitorService.TryDDCWriteTransportProbe\nuses LastKnownBrightnessMax\nand last verified projected bus value] as D18B
  D18X -[#green]- D18A : shared scaling
  D18X -[#green]- D18B : read-degraded probe no longer\nwrites an arbitrary raw value
}

' ----- DUP-21 PARTIAL: two brightness schedulers own one monitor target -----
package "DUP-21  Normal vs immediate brightness drivers" $TINT_PARTIAL {
  [MonitorService._writeThrottler\nnormal cooldown] as D21A
  [MonitorService._immediateWriteThrottler\nzero cooldown] as D21B
  [MonitorEntry.BrightnessTargetGeneration\nshared correctness arbiter] as D21C
  D21A -[#orange]- D21C : same payload pipeline
  D21B -[#orange]- D21C : same payload pipeline
  note bottom
    Generations make the dual-driver implementation correct,
    but two drivers expand the state space. Plan: add a narrowly
    scoped bypass-next-cooldown enqueue mode to AsyncThrottler,
    then return to one driver per monitor. Keep generations.
  end note
}

' ----- DUP-22 OPEN: recovery repeats full enumeration per candidate -----
package "DUP-22  Recovery enumeration" $TINT_OPEN {
  [DDCRecoveryService\nloops candidate IDs] as D22A
  [MonitorService.TryRecoverMonitor\nfresh TryGetMonitors per ID] as D22B
  D22A -[#red]- D22B : N candidates cause N complete\nCCD / registry / WMI enumerations per tick
  note bottom
    Candidate tasks currently run in parallel for responsiveness.
    Plan: batch IDs against one immutable parent-enumeration snapshot,
    then probe with bounded concurrency. Do not restore collateral
    healthy-row reads or unrestricted cross-adapter DDC I/O.
  end note
}

